@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Recording and timing reliability cleanup
+
+Review the proposed cleanup against these requirements and the repository's engineering guidance.
+
+1. A completed lap retains the track and recording session that owned it when completion was observed, even if setup changes or deactivates while a database operation waits. Best/count and history remain transactional.
+2. History-clear success means its transaction committed. Request success or exhausting a cursor is not durable success; failed clears preserve the prior persistent data and must not reset the live count.
+3. The named 50–100 km/h rolling interval uses exactly those SI speed thresholds, independently of dashboard display units. Existing 45–70 mph and 30–60 mph definitions remain unchanged.
+4. GPS course is clockwise from north. Timing velocity remains east/north: course zero must produce northward velocity so direction-aware crossings retain their documented frame.
+5. Release builds preserve Git-derived application version metadata and the exact requested tag in the descriptor. SDK reuse must retain clean checkout and supported packaging behavior.
+6. Clarifying comments and short change notes are in scope. No new driver features or external services are requested.
